  "correctness": "max_abs_err vs R=1 is 0.0 for EVERY (organ, R) cell -- 32 of 32 exact",
  "the_optimum_IS_organ_dependent": "R=2 for q_proj, v_proj, o_proj, gate_proj, down_proj and dn.in_proj_qkv; R=1 for k_proj; R=8 for lm_head. A single global tiling is leaving something on the table at every organ that is not its optimum, which is exactly what this obligation suspected.",
  "lm_head_is_the_outlier": "1.3752 ps/element at R=1 against 0.7209 at R=8 -- a 1.91x gain, and by far the largest in the table. It is also the organ G090 measured as a RISING FLOOR (3.50% of the token now, 10.62% with a free body), so the one organ where geometry pays most is the one whose share grows.",
  "small_organs_are_launch_bound": "k_proj and v_proj at 1024 rows cost 3.86-4.03 ps/element against 1.37-1.60 for the large organs -- 2.5x worse per element purely from being small. Increasing R makes them WORSE (up to 6.01 at R=8) because there are not enough rows to fill the tiles.",
  "a_correction_to_a_standing_figure": "This campaign has quoted 0.8425 ps/element as the q4 GEMV rate. That figure comes from a 4 GiB SYNTHETIC payload with 1,677,720 rows. NO REAL ORGAN except lm_head reaches it: gate_proj is 1.4628 at its best R, q_proj 1.5265, down_proj 1.6114. The headline rate is a large-payload best case, and per-organ costs are 1.7-1.9x higher.",
  "projection_not_measurement": "The acceptance asks for a measured end-to-end win with token-identical output OR a receipt proving the incumbent is already optimal per organ. This delivers neither yet: it proves the incumbent is NOT optimal per organ (the best R differs by organ and lm_head gains 1.91x), but the end-to-end win requires binding per-organ R in the decode path and measuring paired 3/3 with token identity.",
  "commit": "116855c0f2e38632ea177d9c00b783f98500792a",
  "units_correction": "A first pass divided picoseconds by 1e6 instead of 1e9 and printed a 41,140 ms token. Corrected below. The gain RATIOS were unaffected; only the absolute ms were.",
  "isolated_totals": {
    "ms_R1": 41.14033480734253,
    "ms_best": 39.14888746015625,
    "ratio": 1.0508685553124102,
    "measured_production_gemv_ms": 21.587,
    "overstatement_x": 1.9057921344949522
  },
  "the_sum_does_not_close_and_that_is_the_finding": "Summing the isolated per-organ timings gives 41.140 ms of GEMV against a measured 21.587 ms in production -- isolated timings OVERSTATE by 1.91x. Each kernel here is dispatched alone with its own timestamp and a cold command buffer, while production batches 964 dispatches into one. So this sweep is a RANKING instrument and not an additive budget, which is the same law the ledger already recorded when argmax transferred 0 of 0.326 ms. Scaling the isolated saving by the same factor gives 1.045 ms, 3.43% of the token -- and even that is a projection, not a measurement."
